Isoform APP695 is the predominant form in neuronal tissue, isoform APP751 and isoform APP770 are widely expressed in non-neuronal cells. Isoform APP751 is the most abundant form in T-lymphocytes. Appican is expressed in astrocytes","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"12859342","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12859342","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/12859342"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"1406936","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1406936","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/1406936"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"2649245","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2649245","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/2649245"}}]}]},{"type":"INDUCTION","text":[{"value":"Increased levels during neuronal differentiation"}]},{"type":"DOMAIN","text":[{"value":"The transmembrane helix undergoes a conformation change and unravels partially when bound to PSEN1, facilitating cleavage by PSEN1","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"30630874","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/30630874","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/30630874"}}]}]},{"type":"DOMAIN","text":[{"value":"The basolateral sorting signal (BaSS) is required for sorting of membrane proteins to the basolateral surface of epithelial cells","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"9843960","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9843960","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/9843960"}}]}]},{"type":"DOMAIN","text":[{"value":"The GFLD subdomain binds Cu(2+) ions; this promotes homodimerization","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"25122912","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25122912","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/25122912"}}]}]},{"type":"DOMAIN","text":[{"value":"The NPXY sequence motif found in many tyrosine-phosphorylated proteins is required for the specific binding of the PID domain. However, additional amino acids either N- or C-terminal to the NPXY motif are often required for complete interaction. The PID domain-containing proteins which bind APP require the YENPTY motif for full interaction. These interactions are independent of phosphorylation on the terminal tyrosine residue. The YENPXY site is also involved in clathrin-mediated endocytosis","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"10383380","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10383380","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/10383380"}}]}]},{"type":"DOMAIN","text":[{"value":"The C-terminal region can bind zinc ions; this favors dimerization and formation of higher oligomers","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"26898943","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26898943","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/26898943"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"28570778","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/28570778","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/28570778"}}]}]},{"type":"DOMAIN","text":[{"value":"The OX-2 motif shows some similarity to a region in the N-terminus of CD200/MOX2","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"2649245","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2649245","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/2649245"}}]}]},{"type":"PTM","text":[{"value":"Proteolytically processed under normal cellular conditions. Cleavage either by alpha-secretase, beta-secretase or theta-secretase leads to generation and extracellular release of soluble APP peptides, S-APP-alpha and S-APP-beta, and the retention of corresponding membrane-anchored C-terminal fragments, C80, C83 and C99. Subsequent processing of C80 and C83 by gamma-secretase yields P3 peptides. This is the major secretory pathway and is non-amyloidogenic. Alternatively, presenilin/nicastrin-mediated gamma-secretase processing of C99 releases the amyloid-beta proteins, amyloid-beta protein 40 and amyloid-beta protein 42, major components of amyloid plaques, and the cytotoxic C-terminal fragments, gamma-CTF(50), gamma-CTF(57) and gamma-CTF(59). PSEN1 cleavage is more efficient with C83 than with C99 as substrate (in vitro) (PubMed:30630874). Amyloid-beta protein 40 and Amyloid-beta protein 42 are cleaved by ACE (PubMed:11604391, PubMed:16154999). Many other minor amyloid-beta peptides, amyloid-beta 1-X peptides, are found in cerebral spinal fluid (CSF) including the amyloid-beta X-15 peptides, produced from the cleavage by alpha-secretase and all terminating at Gln-686","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"10656250","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10656250","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/10656250"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"11604391","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11604391","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/11604391"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"16154999","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16154999","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/16154999"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"30630874","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/30630874","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/30630874"}}]}]},{"type":"PTM","text":[{"value":"Proteolytically cleaved by caspases during neuronal apoptosis. Cleavage at Asp-739 by either CASP6, CASP8 or CASP9 results in the production of the neurotoxic C31 peptide and the increased production of amyloid-beta peptides","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"10319819","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10319819","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/10319819"}}]}]},{"type":"PTM","text":[{"value":"N-glycosylated (PubMed:2900137). N- and O-glycosylated (PubMed:2649245). O-glycosylation on Ser and Thr residues with core 1 or possibly core 8 glycans. Partial tyrosine glycosylation (Tyr-681) is found on some minor, short amyloid-beta peptides (amyloid-beta 1-15, 1-16, 1-17, 1-18, 1-19 and 1-20) but not found on amyloid-beta protein 38, amyloid-beta protein 40 nor on amyloid-beta protein 42. Modification on a tyrosine is unusual and is more prevelant in AD patients. Glycans had Neu5AcHex(Neu5Ac)HexNAc-O-Tyr, Neu5AcNeu5AcHex(Neu5Ac)HexNAc-O-Tyr and O-AcNeu5AcNeu5AcHex(Neu5Ac)HexNAc-O-Tyr structures, where O-Ac is O-acetylation of Neu5Ac. Neu5AcNeu5Ac is most likely Neu5Ac 2,8Neu5Ac linked. O-glycosylations in the vicinity of the cleavage sites may influence the proteolytic processing. Appicans are L-APP isoforms with O-linked chondroitin sulfate","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"16335952","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16335952","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/16335952"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"21712440","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21712440","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/21712440"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"22576872","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22576872","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/22576872"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"2649245","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2649245","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/2649245"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"2900137","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2900137","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/2900137"}}]}]},{"type":"PTM","text":[{"value":"Phosphorylation in the C-terminal on tyrosine, threonine and serine residues is neuron-specific (PubMed:10341243). Phosphorylation can affect APP processing, neuronal differentiation and interaction with other proteins (PubMed:10341243). Phosphorylated on Thr-743 in neuronal cells by Cdc5 kinase and Mapk10, in dividing cells by Cdc2 kinase in a cell-cycle dependent manner with maximal levels at the G2/M phase and, in vitro, by GSK-3-beta (PubMed:11146006, PubMed:8131745). The Thr-743 phosphorylated form causes a conformational change which reduces binding of Fe65 family members (PubMed:11517218). In dopaminergic (DA) neurons, phosphorylation on Thr-743 by LRKK2 promotes the production and the nuclear translocation of the APP intracellular domain (AICD) which induces DA neuron apoptosis (PubMed:28720718). Phosphorylation on Tyr-757 is required for SHC binding (PubMed:11877420). Phosphorylated in the extracellular domain by casein kinases on both soluble and membrane-bound APP. This phosphorylation is inhibited by heparin (PubMed:8999878)","evidences":[{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"10341243","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10341243","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/10341243"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"11146006","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11146006","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/11146006"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"11517218","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11517218","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/11517218"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"11877420","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11877420","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/11877420"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"28720718","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/28720718","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/28720718"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"8131745","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8131745","alternativeUrl":"https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/8131745"}},{"code":"ECO:0000269","source":{"name":"PubMed","id":"8999878","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8999878","alternativeUrl